        "description": "This course is a basic course for university undergraduate students covering concepts in Newtonian mechanics including rectilinear motion, rigid body rotation, simple harmonic motion, damped oscillations, projectiles, circular motion. Other concepts covered in this course the conservation of energy, linear momentum and angular momentum, phase-plane analysis and the concept of limit cycles. More advanced topics include study of motion via variational principles such as Hamilton\u2019s equation, as well as tensor algebra.",
